<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian retail sales rise 0.7 pct in Nov.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian retail sales rise 0.7 pct in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian retail sales rose 0.7 percent to A$10.24 billion in November, seasonally adjusted, after rising (a revised) 1.2 percent to A$10.12 billion in October, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In November 1995, retail sales rose 0.9 percent to A$9.99 billion.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected retail sales to rise a median 1.0 percent in November.  </p>
<p>Australian retail sales, November (A$ billion)</p>
<p>			  Nov 96  Oct 96 mo/mo pct Nov 95  yr/yr pct</p>
<p>    Seasonally adj   10.24   10.17   +0.7     9.99     +2.4</p>
<p>    Unadjusted	 10.61   10.41   +2.0    10.41     +1.9</p>
<p>    Trend Estimate   10.19   10.22   -0.2    10.00     +1.9</p>
<p>Retail turnover by group percentage change, seasonally adj.</p>
<p>				Nov 96	 Oct 96	 Nov 95</p>
<p>Food retailing	     +0.4	   +0.7	   +1.5</p>
<p>Department stores	  +6.2	   +3.4	   +1.0</p>
<p>Clothing, soft goods     -0.3	   -0.4	   +1.3</p>
<p>Household goods	    -0.3	   +1.7	   -0.8</p>
<p>Recreational goods	 +0.6	   +1.2	   +0.1</p>
<p>Other retailing	    -0.2	   +4.7	   -1.4</p>
<p>Hospitality, services     0.0	   -0.5	   +1.6</p>
<p>Total			  +0.7	   +1.2	   +0.9</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
